<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>Mountaineers Draw With No. 11 South Carolina</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-soccer-mountaineers-draw-with-no-11-south-carolina</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-soccer-mountaineers-draw-with-no-11-south-carolina</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Isaac Scheer battles for the ball against South Carolina" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – In a top-20 matchup at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium, the No. 16 West Virginia University men's soccer team and No. 11 South Carolina played to a 1-1 draw, Saturday night. The Mountaineers go to 5-1-3 this season and 1-0-2 in the Sun Belt while the Gamecocks are now 7-1-2 and 1-0-2 as well in conference play.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg"><media:title>Isaac Scheer battles for the ball against South Carolina</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:47:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59482</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Beat Penn State for First Time Since 2010, Drop Meet to Virginia Tech</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-swimming-diving-mountaineers-beat-penn-state-for-first-time-since-2010-drop-meet-to-virginia-tech</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-swimming-diving-mountaineers-beat-penn-state-for-first-time-since-2010-drop-meet-to-virginia-tech</guid><category>Men's Swimming &amp; Diving</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Two WVU men's swimmers flex their muscles while at practice." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University men's swimming and diving team picked up a win against Penn State for the first time since 2010 and lost to No. 11 Virginia Tech at the Christiansburg Aquatic Center in Christiansburg, Virginia, on Saturday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg"><media:title>Two WVU men's swimmers flex their muscles while at practice.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:26:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>7</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59481</s:story_id></item><item><title>Cyclones Win Big 12 Shootout</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/football-cyclones-win-big-12-shootout</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/football-cyclones-win-big-12-shootout</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Cyrus Trough makes a first-quarter touchdown catch in West Virginia's game played against Iowa State in Ames, Iowa, on Saturday, Oct. 3, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/Traugh-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />Neither team could stop the other, but Iowa State's defense managed to come up with a critical late turnover to turn away West Virginia 45-42 in a back-and-forth, Saturday afternoon Big 12 affair at sunny Jack Trice Stadium in Ames, Iowa.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/Traugh-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/Traugh-Main.jpg"><media:title>Cyrus Trough makes a first-quarter touchdown catch in West Virginia's game played against Iowa State in Ames, Iowa, on Saturday, Oct. 3, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/Traugh-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:17:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59480</s:story_id></item><item><title>Muller Hits Second Straight 600 as Mountaineers Down Army</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/rifle-muller-hits-second-straight-600-as-mountaineers-down-army</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/rifle-muller-hits-second-straight-600-as-mountaineers-down-army</guid><category>Rifle</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Rifle against Mount A" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/DSC07615.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University rifle team notched its first Great America Rifle Conference win of the season, defeating Army 4750-4665 on Saturday inside the Tronsrue Marksmanship Center.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/DSC07615.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/DSC07615.jpg"><media:title>WVU Rifle against Mount A</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/DSC07615.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:39:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>8</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59479</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Welcome Houston to Morgantown for Sunday Matchup</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/volleyball-mountaineers-welcome-houston-to-morgantown-for-sunday-matchup</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/volleyball-mountaineers-welcome-houston-to-morgantown-for-sunday-matchup</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia plays against Houston on Oct. 4 at home" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/VB26_Matchup_1920x1080_houston.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (9-4, 2-1 Big 12) plays host to Houston on Sunday, Oct. 4, at Hope Coliseum. First serve is set for 1 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/VB26_Matchup_1920x1080_houston.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/VB26_Matchup_1920x1080_houston.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia plays against Houston on Oct. 4 at home</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/VB26_Matchup_1920x1080_houston.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:21:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59478</s:story_id></item><item><title>FINAL: West Virginia Falls to Iowa State, 45-42</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/football-game-day-mountaineers-head-to-ames-for-first-true-road-test-against-isu</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/football-game-day-mountaineers-head-to-ames-for-first-true-road-test-against-isu</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Quarterback Michael Hawkins Jr. (3) against Iowa State at Jack Trice Stadium in Ames, Iowa, on Oct. 3, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/920242670-fb_wvuvisu_oct3_2026_js-3.jpg" /><br /><br />AMES, IOWA — West Virginia lost to Iowa State, 45-42, at Jack Trice Stadium in Ames, Iowa, on Oct. 3, 2026.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/920242670-fb_wvuvisu_oct3_2026_js-3.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/920242670-fb_wvuvisu_oct3_2026_js-3.jpg"><media:title>Quarterback Michael Hawkins Jr. (3) against Iowa State at Jack Trice Stadium in Ames, Iowa, on Oct. 3, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/920242670-fb_wvuvisu_oct3_2026_js-3.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:45:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59471</s:story_id></item><item><title>Countdown to Kickoff: Mountaineers, Cyclones to Meet Today in Ames</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-cyclones-to-meet-today-in-ames</link><guid>https://wvusports.co